<title>NORWAY: Elkem 1996 net profits fall.</title>
<headline>Elkem 1996 net profits fall.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31.</p>
<p>				  (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating income		  9,334	vs     9,320</p>
<p> Operating result		  1,024	vs     1,135</p>
<p> Pre-tax result			945	vs     1,079</p>
<p> After-tax result		    736	vs	 850</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Norwegian metals producer is Elkem ASA. A Reuter poll of nine analysts forecast operating profits at 1.04 billion crowns and a result before tax of 940 million crowns. Five of the analysts recommended a sell on the stock, two said hold and two said buy.  </p>
<p>Share of income from</p>
<p>    associated companies	    43	vs	 130</p>
<p> Tax/minorities			205	vs minus 229</p>
<p>NOTE - The board said it would propose a dividend for 1996 of five crowns per share, up from 4.50 crowns in 1995.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
